Employee Management System

A RESTful backend application built with Java and Spring Boot to manage employee records using MySQL.

Features

- Create, read, update, and delete employee records (CRUD)
- Store employee data in a MySQL database
- Validate employee names, email addresses, and salaries
- Handle errors with appropriate HTTP status codes
- Prevent duplicate employee email addresses
- Paginate and sort employee records
- Document and test API endpoints using Swagger UI
- Unit tests for service-layer logic

Technologies Used

- Language: Java 21
- Framework: Spring Boot
- Database: MySQL
- Data Access: Spring Data JPA / Hibernate
- Build Tool: Maven
- API Documentation: Swagger UI / OpenAPI
- Testing: JUnit and Mockito
- Version Control: Git and GitHub

API Endpoints

Method| Endpoint| Description
GET| "/employees"| Get paginated employee records
GET| "/employees/{id}"| Get an employee by ID
POST| "/employees"| Create an employee
PUT| "/employees/{id}"| Update an employee
DELETE| "/employees/{id}"| Delete an employee

Pagination and Sorting

Example:

"GET /employees?page=0&size=5&sortBy=name"

- "page": Page number, starting from 0
- "size": Number of records per page
- "sortBy": Field to sort by, such as "id", "name", "email", or "salary"

Prerequisites

- Java 21 or compatible JDK
- MySQL Server
- Maven, or the included Maven wrapper

Setup and Run

1. Clone the repository:
   
   git clone https://github.com/Chinmayee666ck/EmployeeManagementSystem.git

2. Open the project in IntelliJ IDEA.

3. Create a MySQL database:
   
   CREATE DATABASE employee_db;

4. Configure your local database connection in "src/main/resources/application.properties". Set the database URL, username, and password for your environment. Do not commit credentials to GitHub.

5. Run the application from IntelliJ, or use the Maven wrapper on Windows:
   
   .\mvnw.cmd spring-boot:run

6. Open Swagger UI using the port configured for your application:
   
   "http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui/index.html"
   
   If your application runs on another port, replace "8080" with that port.

Testing

Run the tests with the Maven wrapper:

.\mvnw.cmd test

Error Handling

The API handles common errors, including invalid input, missing employee records, and duplicate email addresses, using appropriate HTTP status codes.

